{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# DC segmenting MD→wiki renderer module (pure capability; codec untouched)\n\n## Context / Problem\nJira Data Center stores rich text as wiki markup (REST v2), a lossy text format.\nThe `RichTextCodec` seam (epic e369, story J3) routes DC rich text through\n`WikiTextCodec` (`adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py:72`), today an **identity**\ncodec: `fit_outbound` (`:82`), `normalize_outbound` (`:96`), `to_wire` (`:100`),\n`decode_inbound` (`:104`) all pass the plain string through. So DC ships rebar's\nraw Markdown as literal wiki source — `# Heading` reads as a hash.\n\nWhole-body conversion is not an option: rebar prose is punctuation-dense and\npandoc's jira reader/writer mangles it. Verified on pandoc 3.6.1 in this\nworktree: a prose `->` is escaped to `\\->`; a Markdown table delimiter row comes\nback as `| \\-\\-\\- |`; punctuation inside inline code is escaped (`` `->` `` →\n`{{\\->}}`); and an HTML comment is **deleted outright** (a lone\n`<!-- rebar:reconciler-echo -->` renders to the empty string) — which would\ndestroy rebar's own reconciler echo marker.\n\nSo the renderer **segments**: convert only structurally-safe units, pass\ndangerous ones through verbatim.\n\n**Why a pure module, not a codec change.** On DC the live outbound wire flows\nTHROUGH a codec op (`OutboundFieldMapper` composes `normalize_outbound(fit_outbound(v))`;\nthe mapper is constructed with `WikiTextCodec` at `jira_datacenter/backend.py:89`).\nSo changing `to_wire`/`normalize_outbound` IS an immediate live cutover, and would\nbreak the pinned identity tests (`test_rich_text_codec.py:244`, `:251`, `:183`) and\nthe codec law (`:163`). The cutover must land WITH echo-safety, which is story\n3388's job. **This story ships only the pure renderer + tests and leaves\n`WikiTextCodec` fully identity.** Nothing observable changes on merge.\n\n## Corpus fixture — RE-SCOPED (premise correction)\nThe original plan cited counts (179 code-arrow bodies, 70 erosion bodies,\n68%/78% coverage) from a 2026-08-03 export. **That export no longer exists** — no\n`parity_*.py`, no `parity-results.md`, no exported corpus, on disk or in git\nhistory; rebar has no file-attachment store, so those `files/…` paths were an\nephemeral session workspace. The numbers are unreproducible and unauditable, so\nthey are replaced by numbers measured from a **committed** fixture.\n\n`.pre-commit-config.yaml` enforces `check-added-large-files` at 500 KB/file, there\nis no LFS, and `.gitignore` records a decision NOT to raise that cap — so the full\n~5.9 MB body set cannot be vendored. The fixture is therefore a **stratified\nsample** built by a committed generator, `scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py`\n(deterministic seed; scrub-then-write, per `scripts/capture_jira_fixtures.py`\ndoctrine): every body exhibiting a phenomenon the renderer must be safe on, plus a\nprose sample. Committed as `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/{code_arrow,table,prose}.json`\n— 29 / 29 / 120 bodies, 178 total, each shard ≤127 KB.\n\n## Approach\n`adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py` exposing `render_markdown_to_wiki(md) -> str`,\n**not referenced by any codec op or live send path in this story**.\n\nSplit into blank-line blocks (fences kept whole) → classify each → render safe\nunits via the wheel-bundled pandoc (`-f commonmark -t jira --wrap=none`) → pass\ndangerous units verbatim → reassemble preserving original order and spacing.\n\nFour lossless rules, each forced by measured pandoc behavior:\n- **Code-aware arrow substitution** (`-> <- <-> =>` → `→ ← ↔ ⇒`) on the Markdown\n  BEFORE pandoc, skipping fenced/inline code. The HTML-comment delimiters `<!--`\n  and `-->` are matched first and mapped to themselves, so `-->` is never rewritten\n  to `-→`.\n- **ASCII tables wrapped verbatim in `{noformat}`**, never converted.\n- **HTML-comment and HTML/regex-dense blocks emitted verbatim** (pandoc deletes\n  comments).\n- **Post-render code-preservation check**: after converting a unit, every code\n  fragment of the source must appear verbatim in the output; otherwise that unit\n  falls back to its original Markdown. This turns pandoc's unpredictable escaping\n  into a safe fallback instead of silent corruption.\n\nA unit that already looks like wiki (`h1.`, `{code}`, `{{…}}`) is passed through,\nso a Jira-authored body is never re-rendered as Markdown.\n\n**pandoc delivery.** Pin `pypandoc-binary==1.15` (bundles pandoc in the wheel) as a\nnew `wiki` extra + in `dev` so CI exercises it. If pandoc is absent or a unit fails,\nthe renderer returns input unchanged (echo-safe, never corrupting).\n\n`jira_family/` imports nothing from `adapters/jira/`\n(`docs/adr/0083-reconciler-vendor-adapter-seam.md`), and pandoc is not a Cloud\ndependency, so the renderer belongs here.\n\n## Scope\n- `adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py` (new) — the segmenting renderer.\n- `scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py` (new) + `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/` (new).\n- `pyproject.toml` — `wiki` extra + dev pin; `src/rebar/_optional.py` — register it.\n- `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py` — exclude the fixture (captured data, not\n  authored text).\n- **UNCHANGED:** `WikiTextCodec` and all its ops; `jira_datacenter/backend.py:154\n  normalize_rich_text`; every live send site (all wired by 3388).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `render_markdown_to_wiki` renders safe units to wiki and passes dangerous\n  units (tables, HTML-dense, regex-dense) verbatim, preserving order; verified by\n  `test_dc_segmenting_passthrough`.\n- [ ] Arrow substitution runs before pandoc, converts prose arrows, and rewrites\n  **zero** code arrows; `-->` is never corrupted; verified by\n  `test_dc_arrow_substitution_spares_code` and `test_arrow_substitution_cases`.\n- [ ] Over all 178 committed corpus bodies, **zero** arrow-bearing code fragments\n  are lost; verified by `test_dc_corpus_no_code_arrow_is_ever_rewritten`.\n- [ ] ASCII tables are `{noformat}`-wrapped and all 31 corpus table bodies still\n  contain a table after rendering; verified by `test_dc_table_noformat_stable` and\n  `test_dc_corpus_tables_survive_verbatim`.\n- [ ] Every HTML comment in the corpus survives rendering (pandoc deletes them);\n  verified by `test_dc_corpus_html_comments_survive`.\n- [ ] Rendering is deterministic across repeated passes, and an already-wiki body\n  passes through unchanged; verified by\n  `test_dc_corpus_render_is_deterministic_across_passes` and\n  `test_dc_already_wiki_body_passes_through`.\n- [ ] `pypandoc-binary` is pinned and, when pandoc is unavailable,\n  `render_markdown_to_wiki` returns its input unchanged; verified by\n  `test_dc_pandoc_absent_identity` and `test_dc_pandoc_failure_degrades_that_unit`.\n- [ ] Corpus richness: ≥90% of bodies and ≥95% of characters render rich (measured\n  92.7% / 98.4%); the fixture cardinality is pinned at 178; verified by\n  `test_dc_corpus_coverage` and `test_corpus_cardinality_is_pinned`.\n- [ ] The committed fixture carries no unscrubbed emails, tenant hostnames or URLs;\n  verified by `test_corpus_carries_no_unscrubbed_secrets`.\n- [ ] `WikiTextCodec` stays identity and no live send site changes; verified by the\n  existing `test_wiki_normalize_is_identity`,\n  `test_wiki_codec_wire_shape_and_decode_are_the_plain_string`,\n  `test_non_string_values_pass_through_untouched` and the codec-law test staying\n  green unmodified."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786569617945658001,"uuid":"9808076a-3072-4b18-bb41-179ce2b05fce"}